WEBVTT

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:02.910
The Digital World,

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:06.090
a world inhabited by unusual 
creatures called Digimon.

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:09.950
It has been conquered 
by the evil Bagra Army

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:14.490
and divided into seven Kingdoms 
ruled by seven Death Generals.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.230
Taiki Kudou has leapt 
into these seven Kingdoms

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:22.050
along with his partner, 
Shoutmon, to save the Digimon.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.690
This is the story of the 
friendship and adventures

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:28.540
shared by Taiki, his friends, 
and the Digimon.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:55.930
We won in the battle against Yuu 
in the hellish realm, Hell's Field,

00:01:55.930 --> 00:02:00.570
but Lilithmon, burning for revenge, 
became an evil beast and attacked us.

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:05.140
She began to destroy Hell's 
Field and everyone in it.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:09.540
Through a desperate plan, 
we just barely managed to escape,

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:13.780
but in his effort to protect 
us all, Beelzebumon was...

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:19.280
Beelzebumon?

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:21.670
Thank you, Taiki.

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:25.970
Don't forget that I'm with you.

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:30.340
Beelzebumon...

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:35.670
Beelzebumon!

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:44.690
<b>Taiki's Decision!</b>

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:44.690
<b>Surpass Apollomon, the Strongest of All!</b>

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:39.450
Taiki's Decision!

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.810
Surpass Apollomon, the Strongest of All!

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:57.090
What have I done?

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:01.730
So you understand what we've done now.

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:03.650
We?

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:06.830
You... Are you saying you used my body

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:08.730
to destroy Taiki and his companions?

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:12.490
That's exactly what I'm saying.

00:03:12.490 --> 00:03:16.910
We're number two in the Bagra Army now,

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:19.450
since I made sure Admiral DarkKnightmon

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:23.010
and his General, Yuu, 
were taken down with them.

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:28.750
Taiki... I'm sorry.

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:35.160
Gate Open!

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:44.000
Yuu!

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:46.770
So DarkKnightmon's headed back 
to the Great Bagra Palace?

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:50.340
We'll have to defeat Apollomon Whispered,

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:51.940
or we can't go after Yuu.

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:54.030
What do we do, Taiki?

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:55.710
Taiki! Taiki!

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:58.720
About the analysis you asked me for,

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:02.050
of whether Apollomon and 
Whispered can be separated...

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:04.190
I'll start with my conclusion.

00:04:04.190 --> 00:04:08.160
There is no way to remove 
Whispered from Apollomon.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:12.510
Apollomon and Whispered 
are one and the same,

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:15.130
a single Digimon with two hearts.

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:20.420
It's likely that Bagramon 
rewrote Apollomon's program

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:22.940
when he made him a Death General.

00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:28.140
Whispered's data is closely 
connected to Apollomon's data.

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:32.770
If one of them is lost, 
both will be destroyed.

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:33.900
I see.

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:35.920
Thanks, Wisemon.

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:37.460
I'm sorry to bring bad news.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:44.630
There's only one solution.

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:50.340
I made my decision while 
I was fighting with Yuu,

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:55.310
and my resolve hardened even more 
when I saw Beelzebumon fall.

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:24.020
Let's go.

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:31.260
Find a place where we can break in.

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:32.980
With pleasure!

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:38.020
Hey, Miss Mervamon.

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:41.060
I, uh...

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:45.190
I'm not really good at saying the 
right thing at times like these...

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:51.280
But we all loved Beelzebumon, too.

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:52.960
Shoutmon...

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:57.660
We'll build a world where no one 
will ever feel this sad again.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:59.120
That's a promise!

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:00.750
So let's see a smile!

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:04.900
That's what would make Beelzebumon 
happier than anything.

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:08.280
I got it.

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:15.010
He's a big man, for such a little guy.

00:06:15.010 --> 00:06:18.120
Yeah, it's the one thing 
he's got going for him.

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:22.090
They're going somewhere, General!

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:30.720
All the soldiers are 
headed beneath the tower.

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:34.710
Whispered still doesn't 
know we've come back?

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:37.910
All right, then...

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:48.150
Foolish citizens, I am Apollomon,

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:50.100
the god of this Kingdom.

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:52.690
I'm in a great mood today,

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:56.750
so I think I'll set you all free.

00:06:56.750 --> 00:07:01.070
Yes, free from your suffering... forever.

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:05.940
Your bodies themselves will become 
negative power and disappear,

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:08.840
so that you can be useful 
to Lord Bagramon.

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:10.510
B-But...

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:13.180
I'll take away your pain now.

00:07:13.180 --> 00:07:15.310
Give thanks to your god!

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:16.510
Stop!

00:07:16.510 --> 00:07:19.000
After waging such an unjust war,

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:22.720
you would make the innocent 
citizens suffer even more?

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:25.440
Being weak is a sin.

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:27.890
Now is a good time to return 
to the Great Bagra Palace.

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:31.100
A little cleanup is just 
what the doctor ordered.

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:34.100
Help!

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:38.970
What?!

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:43.190
An evil king has no right 
to call himself a god!

00:07:43.510 --> 00:07:44.590
Greymon!

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:48.350
MailBirdramon!

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:51.420
DigiXros!

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:54.520
MetalGreymon!

00:07:54.520 --> 00:07:56.310
Insufferable jerks!

00:07:56.310 --> 00:07:59.040
Seeing ruffians like them 
makes my blood boil!

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:00.350
Same here!

00:08:00.350 --> 00:08:02.430
Strike them down!

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:04.000
MetalGreymon!

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:05.330
Digivolve!

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:11.140
MetalGreymon, Digivolve!

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:14.270
ZekeGreymon!

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:16.870
Mervamon!

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:19.940
Sparrowmon!

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:22.450
DigiXros!

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:25.320
JetMervamon!

00:08:26.620 --> 00:08:29.250
What?! It can't be!

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:36.430
They're still alive?

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:39.930
Then... could Taiki Kudou also be...

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:47.410
No! They headed here while we 
were only lightly defended!

00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:49.490
Taiki!

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:55.610
Drill Buster!

00:08:57.220 --> 00:09:00.430
Their defenses are weak. 
You were right, Taiki.

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:02.550
They think we're dead.

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:04.090
This way!

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:11.030
It appears throwing them into 
hell was a mistake, Whispered.

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:12.100
What?!

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:15.130
It only made them stronger.

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:20.030
Taiki and his companions rose 
up from hell with new strength.

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:24.540
The day when all of us Death 
Generals fall has come at last.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:25.960
Nonsense!

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:28.850
He's here! It's Taiki!

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:31.840
You'd best prepare yourself, Whispered!

00:09:35.020 --> 00:09:36.040
No, wait...

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.820
Apollomon! That form is...

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:08.650
<i>Yuu! Yuu!</i>

00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:10.430
<i>Yuu!</i>

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:14.030
<i>Yuu! Where are you?</i>

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:15.930
<i>Yuu!</i>

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:20.710
<i>Oh, I finally found you.</i>

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:24.090
<i>Who are you?</i>

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:25.880
<i>Me Damemon.</i>

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:27.360
<i>What you name?</i>

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:28.810
<i>Yuu.</i>

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:29.730
<i>Huh?</i>

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:31.980
<i>No. You name.</i>

00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:37.050
<i>It's Yuu. My name is Yuu Amano.</i>

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:39.670
<i>Huh? You name is Yuu?</i>

00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:41.510
<i>Oh! Amazing!</i>

00:10:41.510 --> 00:10:43.390
<i>What a wonderful name!</i>

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:50.060
<i>What's wrong, Yuu?</i>

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:54.050
<i>My grandma died today.</i>

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:55.280
<i>Oh...</i>

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:57.240
<i>Grandma...</i>

00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:01.720
<i>Can't help it, Yuu.</i>

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:03.740
<i>Living things die someday.</i>

00:11:03.740 --> 00:11:06.510
<i>Nobody can stop it.</i>

00:11:09.010 --> 00:11:10.250
<i>Interesting.</i>

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:13.660
<i>Yuu.</i>

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:20.990
<i>Would you like to come play 
in a land where nobody dies?</i>

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:23.360
<i>Is there such a place?</i>

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:24.930
<i>Indeed, there is.</i>

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:28.880
<i>I'm preparing lots of 
fun things there now.</i>

00:11:29.510 --> 00:11:34.220
<i>I believe you'll be ready to come and 
play when you've grown a bit bigger.</i>

00:11:34.220 --> 00:11:37.600
<i>Yeah! I will! I definitely will!</i>

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:43.680
<i>Then, give your name to this Xros Loader.</i>

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:46.220
<i>Yuu Amano.</i>

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:52.010
<i>Can you say "DigiXros" for me?</i>

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:53.420
<i>DigiXros!</i>

00:11:58.060 --> 00:12:00.100
<i>Looks fun, doesn't it?</i>

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:02.830
<i>I promise I'll come back for you.</i>

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:06.280
<i>This will be our little secret.</i>

00:12:06.280 --> 00:12:08.590
<i>Okay, Yuu?</i>

00:12:08.590 --> 00:12:11.090
<i>Yuu? Yuu!</i>

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:13.560
<i>Sis...</i>

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:17.380
<i>Yuu! Thank goodness!</i>

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:32.010
Taiki...

00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:38.200
Oh, Sir Yuu, you're awake.

00:12:38.200 --> 00:12:41.030
Damemon... I...

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:43.820
I let Taiki die!

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:50.320
If the Digital World isn't 
a game world, then I... I...

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:53.360
Sir Yuu...

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:01.730
How cowardly can you get?

00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:07.040
That's right. This is a trap.

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:09.580
He switched his body for mine,

00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:12.270
knowing your heart would 
be too kind to kill me.

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:13.700
Well?

00:13:13.700 --> 00:13:19.610
Can you attack your friend 
Apollomon, Taiki Kudou?

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:21.960
Die as you deliberate!

00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:24.500
Let's go, everyone!

00:13:24.710 --> 00:13:26.420
Star Blade!

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:29.090
Ultimate Speaker!

00:13:29.090 --> 00:13:30.420
Drill Buster!

00:13:30.420 --> 00:13:31.060
What?!

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:36.460
I don't believe it! You attacked me?!

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:37.520
Taiki!

00:13:38.810 --> 00:13:39.730
Shoutmon!

00:13:39.730 --> 00:13:41.770
Digivolve!

00:13:42.570 --> 00:13:45.230
Shoutmon, Digivolve!

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:48.740
OmegaShoutmon!

00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:51.060
Hard Rock Damashi!

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:54.450
You...

00:13:54.450 --> 00:13:57.850
Taiki Kudou, why?!

00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:01.510
I couldn't defeat Apollomon back then...

00:14:01.510 --> 00:14:04.390
because I was naive and weak.

00:14:04.390 --> 00:14:09.820
I needed to bear the pain of defeating 
Apollomon, for his own sake, too!

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:15.230
I realized that when I 
fought Yuu in Hell's Field.

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:16.860
I will bear it...

00:14:16.860 --> 00:14:18.220
And I will fight!

00:14:20.570 --> 00:14:22.090
Kiriha! Nene!

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:24.910
We saved all the trapped Digimon!

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:27.600
Looks like you've got it now, Taiki.

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:32.250
True strength that's not only kind, 
but stern when necessary!

00:14:34.360 --> 00:14:35.800
Let's go, everyone!

00:14:36.190 --> 00:14:37.820
Great Xros!

00:14:39.820 --> 00:14:41.310
OmegaShoutmon!

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:42.160
Okay!

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:43.530
ZekeGreymon!

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:46.030
Ballistamon!

00:14:46.930 --> 00:14:48.130
Dorulumon!

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:50.080
Starmons!

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:51.330
Yes!

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:53.710
Sparrowmon!

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:55.410
Great Xros!

00:15:00.970 --> 00:15:03.830
Shoutmon X7!

00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:07.070
Double Flare Buster!

00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:16.430
Don't get too confident.

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:20.830
You think my strength is limited 
because of this right arm

00:15:20.830 --> 00:15:25.000
that Apollomon injured and 
left immobile, don't you?

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:29.540
This...

00:15:29.540 --> 00:15:30.710
X7!

00:15:30.710 --> 00:15:31.510
Smash it!

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:38.020
You can all disappear 
along with Bright Land,

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:40.400
by my ultimate technique...

00:15:42.350 --> 00:15:44.990
The Sun of Lamentation.

00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:49.610
You'll be okay now.

00:15:55.410 --> 00:15:57.460
This is the end.

00:15:57.460 --> 00:15:59.970
All in this Kingdom will burn to ashes!

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:04.190
Die!

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:06.240
Vanish without a trace!

00:16:06.580 --> 00:16:12.550
All of your death data will be converted 
to negative energy and reused.

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:15.150
Be grateful.

00:16:16.130 --> 00:16:17.460
Have you found it yet, Dracomon?

00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:18.930
I've got it!

00:16:18.930 --> 00:16:21.080
Mervamon, pierce it here with your sword!

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:27.530
You did it!

00:16:30.070 --> 00:16:30.800
Yeah!

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:32.140
Hurry, X7!

00:16:32.140 --> 00:16:32.720
Right!

00:16:35.240 --> 00:16:37.840
It's huge! How big is this thing?!

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:43.970
You're too late.

00:16:43.970 --> 00:16:46.280
It's already complete.

00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:48.650
All I have to do now is throw it.

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:49.850
It's over!

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:50.690
Stop!

00:16:50.690 --> 00:16:52.360
Take this!

00:16:53.790 --> 00:16:55.700
The sun is falling!

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:56.780
Help!

00:16:58.900 --> 00:17:01.030
Seven Victorize!

00:17:09.220 --> 00:17:13.650
Trying to stop the Sun of Lamentation 
with such a technique is foolish.

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:16.480
You can't even put a scratch on it!

00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:17.770
There!

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:25.590
Come on...

00:17:25.590 --> 00:17:27.540
Come on, X7!

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:29.190
Don't lose!

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:30.260
Dorulumon!

00:17:30.680 --> 00:17:32.610
Shoutmon!

00:17:33.230 --> 00:17:35.430
Keep it up, everyone!

00:17:35.430 --> 00:17:38.790
Go, X7!

00:17:38.790 --> 00:17:39.870
You can do it!

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:41.770
X7!

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:44.340
We'll do our best, too! Hang in there!

00:17:45.320 --> 00:17:46.400
You can do it!

00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:48.210
Don't lose!

00:17:49.150 --> 00:17:51.500
Time to put an end to this.

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:52.220
Farewell.

00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:57.150
What?!

00:17:57.150 --> 00:17:58.640
Impossible!

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:00.890
This right arm shouldn't be able to move!

00:18:04.130 --> 00:18:05.660
Apollomon...

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:20.080
X7!

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:24.320
Seven Victorize Maximum!

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:42.550
Yeah!

00:18:41.210 --> 00:18:42.550
He did it!

00:18:50.360 --> 00:18:52.900
The whole world should have been mine...

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:56.070
It's not fair.

00:19:02.850 --> 00:19:04.370
Apollomon...

00:19:05.840 --> 00:19:08.240
You did it, Taiki.

00:19:08.660 --> 00:19:11.180
Peace has returned to the Kingdom.

00:19:11.180 --> 00:19:12.140
Yeah...

00:19:12.700 --> 00:19:17.420
But they're all celebrating, 
thinking the evil king has fallen.

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:20.070
None of them know you have a just heart.

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:22.140
It doesn't matter...

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:24.920
As long as you know.

00:19:24.920 --> 00:19:27.850
I truly thank you.

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:34.170
You have defeated all of the 
seven powerful Death Generals.

00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:37.820
It is time to enter the 
Great Bagra Palace.

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:41.680
Do not be complacent. 
Bagramon is a formidable foe.

00:19:42.140 --> 00:19:46.360
He is attempting to reformat 
and brainwash all Digimon

00:19:46.360 --> 00:19:48.170
to follow his commands.

00:19:49.420 --> 00:19:53.710
For now, he is letting weak Digimon 
live so that he can use them,

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:55.770
but when the preparations 
for D5 are complete,

00:19:56.350 --> 00:20:01.410
he will make all Digimon 
his own servants.

00:20:02.230 --> 00:20:07.300
The future is in your 
hands, young ones...

00:20:25.310 --> 00:20:29.910
Looks like they've saved us the 
trouble of punishing Apollomon.

00:20:33.190 --> 00:20:36.560
This is the end for Yuu, as well.

00:20:37.160 --> 00:20:41.130
I suppose I'll go and 
play with them next...

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:44.500
with the new idea I've 
been saving for them.

00:20:49.630 --> 00:20:51.350
Sir Yuu...

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:53.630
No... Yuu.

00:20:53.630 --> 00:20:57.210
I'm sorry I lied to you all this time.

00:20:57.210 --> 00:20:57.740
What?

00:20:57.740 --> 00:21:02.320
But I did it to protect you.

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:04.410
I wanted...

00:21:07.710 --> 00:21:12.620
to protect you... from the cruel reality.

00:21:15.980 --> 00:21:16.890
Damemon!

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:21.040
Damemon!

00:21:21.040 --> 00:21:24.810
But... I couldn't protect you to the end.

00:21:31.030 --> 00:21:33.270
I'm sorry, Yuu.

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:34.740
Damemon...

00:21:34.740 --> 00:21:37.000
No... it can't be!

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:38.820
I'll fix you now!

00:21:39.990 --> 00:21:42.620
Chuchumon! Where's the Darkness Loader?!

00:21:45.490 --> 00:21:47.190
Chuchumon!

00:21:49.170 --> 00:21:50.410
Damemon!

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:54.620
From now on, you will fight alone.

00:21:54.620 --> 00:21:58.430
You mustn't lose...

